From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kara Monk <monkey.ae86@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:21:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x1-microsoft-denali: enable the video
 decoder

The video codec node (iris) inherited from hamoa.dtsi is disabled on the
Surface Pro 11 and has no firmware-name, so the decoder never probes and
hardware video decoding falls back to the CPU.

Enable it and point it at the device-specific signed firmware, as is done for
the other X1E laptops (Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x, Dell XPS 13 9345). The firmware
lives alongside the Denali ADSP and CDSP images, so set it in the shared
x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi.

Measured on a Surface Pro 11 (OLED, X1E-80-100) with hw-test: before, the
hardware decoder gave no frames; after, 60 frames of 720p H.264 decoded on the
hardware decoder in 0.2 s. WebGL and WebGPU measured the same before and after.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
index 230f2da..d54d90d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -1175,6 +1175,12 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&iris {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Denali/qcvss8380.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &lpass_tlmm {
 	spkr_01_sd_n_active: spkr-01-sd-n-active-state {
 		pins = "gpio12";
-- 
2.56.1

